> A model with that many parameters needs (much) more data. Start with a constant model. My own preference is to fit PLB models first and worry about density later, if at all. Also, you seem to have no recaptures (or no spatial recaptures) in session 6, so no info to support session-specific estimates of detection parameters in session 6 (it would help to see the output from summary(quoll_f, terse = T) and perhaps m.array(quoll_f)). There may be other problems, but you should start small.
